WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/onboarding/components/Stepper.tsx — a PURE presentational leaf (prompt: "Data sources:
  (none — pure presentational component)"; shared components used: @/components/ui):
    <ol aria-label="Onboarding steps" class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      {steps.map(step => <li> [ indicator-column(circle + connector) | title + description + while-current CTA ] )}
    stateOf(steps, i): step.done ? 'done' : (firstIndex(!done) === i ? 'current' : 'pending')
       → a satisfied step that FOLLOWS the current step still reads 'done' (own-flag checked first).
    indicator : done → <Check/> (emerald) · current → <Loader2 animate-spin/> (cyan) · pending → numeric {i+1} (muted)
    connector : non-last row; done → emerald/40 else surface-2.   (indicator is aria-hidden)
    title/desc colors per state; CTA renders ONLY while current && step.cta (default <Button variant=primary
       size=sm icon={<ArrowRight/>}>; web Button renders {icon} BEFORE {children} → arrow is LEADING; `disabled`
       supported; `renderCta` render-prop override → a keyed activation in native).
    `OnboardingStep.icon?` is DECLARED in the interface but NEVER read by the component render → faithfully omitted.
  Only ONE string is extracted from the source: the <ol aria-label> "Onboarding steps". Step titles/descriptions
  arrive pre-localized as props (caller data), exactly as on the web — they are not catalog keys.

